# [[.Title]] — built with canguro-rails

> Convention over configuration, so the code goes where you expect it.
> The house rules are in the toolkit:
> **https://github.com/enrand22/canguro-rails/blob/main/CONVENTIONS.md**

## Quickstart

```bash
make setup                  # templ, goose, golangci-lint
cp .env.example .env        # then edit DATABASE_URL and SESSION_SECRET
make db-up                  # MySQL for tests (port 3307)
make migrate                # apply migrations
make test                   # the suite (against the test database)
make run                    # http://localhost:8080
```

## Layout

```
cmd/[[.App]]/            the binary: config → database → jobs → routes → server
internal/config/         declares this app's variables (validated at boot)
internal/models/         the ONLY layer that talks SQL
internal/services/       business rules (tested without HTTP)
internal/controllers/    thin HTTP layer
internal/views/          templ templates
internal/routes/         every route, in one file
internal/health/         the health check that actually checks the database
migrations/              numbered, immutable once applied
web/static/              CSS and JS (the toolkit's assets are used by default)
```

## What the toolkit gives this project

- **htmx + templ**: `web.Render` answers an htmx request with the fragment and
  everyone else with the full page — one handler, not two.
- **Validation without JavaScript**: `RenderInvalid` returns 422 with the form
  re-rendered.
- **Bounded background work**: `jobs` (never a bare `go func()`).
- **Migrations that never run behind your back**: `make migrate`, explicitly.
- **Tests that cannot lie**: a missing database is a failure when `REQUIRE_DB=1`
  (what `make test` sets), and a skip only when nobody asked for it.

## Deploy

`config/deploy.yml` has the Kamal skeleton. Fill in the server, the domain and the
image, then `kamal setup` / `kamal deploy`. The health check points at `/healthz`,
which queries the database on purpose: a 200 that lies is worse than a 500.
